messages:
nina: opened PR 9203 to add a 'latency shading' example to Console observability and cross-language tracing snippets (Java + C#). Also fixed a broken dashboards anchor and updated a YAML sample. need quick docs review.

joel: which YAML key changed? can you paste snippets?

nina: we renamed `latencyBuckets` -> `latency_buckets` in the YAML example to follow snake_case. adding a compat note. Java snippet: 
```java
// Java (redwood-java v0.6+)
RedwoodClient client = new RedwoodClient(System.getenv("REDWOOD_KEY"));
client.attachTrace("trace-xyz", Map.of("route","/v1/generate","model","r-1"), Map.of("latency_buckets", List.of(50,200,500)));
// subsequent call reuses trace context
```

rachel: C# please? I'll run examples in the snippet runner.

nina: C# snippet: 
```csharp
// C# (.NET SDK v1.2)
var client = new RedwoodClient(Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REDWOOD_KEY"));
client.AttachTrace("trace-xyz", new { route = "/v1/generate", model = "r-1" }, new { latency_buckets = new[] { 50, 200, 500 } });
// pass trace into subsequent Generate call
```

docs-bot: link-checker: replaced /docs/dashboards#old-latency-anchor -> /docs/dashboards#latency-shading. verify anchor exists.

joel: tiny nit: add SDK version notes above each snippet (Java v0.6+, C# v1.2+) and show short compatibility YAML with both keys so embedded dashboards don't break.

dave: I'll add a docs-ci lint job that yaml-parses docs/examples/latency_sample.yaml and flags camelCase fields. non-blocking for now.

rachel: ran both snippets after nina's tweak. C# anonymous object needed explicit field names in .NET 6; I pushed a small snippet fix. Also uploaded latency screenshot and added alt text.

nina: pushed fixes: version notes, compat YAML showing both `latency_buckets` and `latencyBuckets` with a deprecation note, alt text, and CI lint job reference in PR. targeting merge after CI.

joel: LGTM once CI passes. thanks all.

docs-bot: ci: docs-ci/latency-yaml-lint succeeded on branch.

nina: merging now. will follow up with a short changelog entry `docs: latency-shading examples (java, csharp)`

joel: thanks!
